---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="HealthDrop Support"
  description="HealthDrop setup and support for iPhone exports and the Android release candidate."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="eyebrow">HealthDrop</div>
    <h1>Support</h1>
    <p class="hero-lede">
      HealthDrop displays health summaries and exports records you permit it
      to read. iPhone and Android features differ. Android 1.4.0 is a release
      candidate and is not yet available on Google Play.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <span class="section-label">iPhone Setup</span>
    <ol>
      <li>Open HealthDrop and grant HealthKit read access.</li>
      <li>Choose iCloud Drive, share sheet, or your own HTTP endpoint.</li>
      <li>Tap Export. iCloud maintains a manifest and daily JSON files using incremental reads; other destinations receive a JSON file.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <span class="section-label">Android Release Candidate</span>
    <ol>
      <li>Use a supported device with Health Connect available.</li>
      <li>Allow the five read categories: steps, resting heart rate, HRV RMSSD, sleep and exercise sessions.</li>
      <li>Run Export to create a fresh snapshot of the last 30 days and open the system share sheet. Cancel the sheet to keep the file local, or choose a recipient only if you intend to share.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>No health-record write, background read, extended-history or automatic health-file upload is requested. iCloud and HTTP endpoint export are not supported in this Android candidate.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <span class="section-label">Automatic Exports and Privacy</span>
    <p>On iPhone, iCloud export can run at launch or resume and through best-effort background tasks. Turning off the launch-export setting does not stop the background iCloud path. Selecting a share-sheet or HTTP target disables automatic iCloud export for that target.</p>
    <p>Production builds use Sentry for technical crash diagnostics and Expo for compatible app updates. See the <a href="/healthdrop/privacy/">privacy policy</a> for data flows and local copies.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <span class="section-label">Troubleshooting</span>
    <p>
      If HealthKit data is missing, check iOS Settings and confirm HealthDrop
      has permission to read the relevant health categories. If iCloud exports
      do not appear immediately, give iCloud Drive a few minutes to sync.
    </p>
    <p>On Android, all five permissions are required before export. If access is denied, export stops before creating a shared file. Check Health Connect permissions and data sources; an empty export does not establish that a source app has synchronized records. Revoke access in the platform health settings when desired.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <span class="section-label">Contact</span>
    <p>
      For issues or questions, contact Hankyeol Kyung through
      <a href="https://github.com/keenranger" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a>
      or <a href="https://x.com/hankyeolkyung" target="_blank" rel="noopener">X</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
